IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 1985 (ACT), Parts 2 and 3 -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- READING (fork F1 in NOTES.md): "a limitation period of N years running from the date when ..." and "brought N years
-- or more after the day ..." are both read with that day excluded (as the Legislation Act 2001 s 151 does; that Act is
-- not deposited): the last day on which the action may be brought is the same date N years on. From 29 February to a
-- year without one, the last day is 28 February. A last day on a weekend or holiday is not moved.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Limitation Act 1985 (ACT), Parts 2 and 3`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The days strictly after one day and strictly before another (none if there are none). With fork F1 a period
-- "running from" a day begins on the next day, so the days on which it runs before a later day are these.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days strictly between` `the start` `and` `the end` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start` MINUS 1
    ELSE 0

-- The day a number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

-- The same date n years on (29 February to 28 February in a year without one).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `years after` `the day` MEANS
    IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
        AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
        AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE a `falls on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

-- The same day n months on (n at most 12); where the later month has no such day, its last day. READING (fork F1):
-- "within 6 months after the day" (s 30A (6)) ends on that day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the days in the month`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) `the month` `the year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY `the days in the month` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS n
        `the month` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN `the month count` MINUS 12
            ELSE `the month count`
        `the year` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1
            ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day`
        `the days in the month` MEANS
            IF `the month` EQUALS 12
            THEN 31
            ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`the month` PLUS 1) `the year`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)
